		<td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=2952&amp;sid=4debcefa8d843ac3b1f04bc767262a52#2952"><img src="templates/subBlack/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Thu Jul 21, 2005 11:19 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: Guild Wars</span></td>
				<td valign="top" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=2952&amp;sid=4debcefa8d843ac3b1f04bc767262a52"><img src="templates/subBlack/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr> 
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Let me just say that I have been playing Guild Wars for a little over three weeks now and it is one of the most fun games I have played in a long time. There is four ways to play: 
<br />

<br />
First you can just get on and play no quests, no mission, no point what-so-ever but to go out and just kill stuff. No group you say? Well GW takes care of that by provding you with four to 8 henchman to go along with you to watch your back. I find this to be one of the best aspects of the game. No waiting around just jump in and start creaming things. Since all zones outside the cities are instanced no messing with dumb people trying to KS you either. 
<br />

<br />
Second, you can do the quests. There are tons of them and again all the above things apply. Quests are mini missions you can do in a little as fifteen minutes to as long as 3 hours some are really simple like find so-and-so and deliver some goods, to go out and kill a mini-boss and destroy his guardians. These can be very tough.
<br />

<br />
Third, there are missions. Man are the missions fun fun fun!!! This is where the game really takes on a whole different tone and scope. Some places on the map are not even opend till you do missions and that is not to say they are closed to you if you don't do them it is really to say that getting to those places are more difficult without them and also you lose the feel of where the game is going and it's point. 
<br />

<br />
Fourth there is a PVP character you can play. You start at level 20 which currently is the highest level you can attain in both the roleplay and PVP areas. I have not tried it so I will leave it to someone else to comment.
<br />

<br />
Finally, I would like to say that I have met up with Noxia from EQ and we have done a small quest together I really enjoyed hanging with her and till she helped me I was not able to complete it because the boss mob was too tough. I said to her, "Boy you made that a lot easier." To which she replied, " It is easier with real people." So that is what I want to end on here I hope that in the future I will see more people from EQ and hopfully they will keep the online free.<br />_________________<br />Darerisk Bloodblighter (Mother always said, "Evil is as evil does , and you my son is EVIL!")
<br />
Darerisk Necro 64
<br />
Pneumo Cleric 57
<br />
Xerk Mage 55
<br />
Ashwarie Druid 55
<br />
Zxerkas Enchanter 50
<br />
Drashra Beastlord 36</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
